;
; PIO program to oversample one ESC's bidirectional-DShot telemetry reply.
;
; After the command frame the CPU switches the motor pin to an input and lets
; this free-running sampler read the line one bit per `in`, autopushing a
; packed 32-bit word every 32 samples. The CPU drains the words captured during
; the reply window, finds the edges, and reconstructs the 21-bit GCR frame for
; the decode in src/libs/Dshot (gcrDifferentialDecode then decodeErpm).
;
; The sample clock (clkdiv) is set to a bench-tuned oversample of the telemetry
; bit rate. The telemetry bit rate, the turnaround delay, and the samples per
; bit are all BENCH-TUNED constants in OutNative.cpp: they cannot be verified
; in simulation and need a logic-analyzer or a real ESC to pin down.

.program dshot_bidir_rx
.wrap_target
    in pins, 1
.wrap
